{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals","id":1561680,"title":"[V20] Vicissitude questions (flaws, other supernaturals)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-14T06:42:18-07:00","id":1561680,"title":"[V20] Vicissitude questions (flaws, other supernaturals)","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> For V20, can you help me answer the following regarding Vicissitude, mainly for Vicissitude 2 and 3, Fleshcraft and Bonecraft:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can/Does Vicissitude fix Flaws?<br /> Seems to me all of these can be remediated: <b>Short, Disfigured, Child, Dulled Bite, Fangless, One Eye, Deformity, Lame, Monstrous, Permanent Fangs</b>, and the aesthetical effects of <b>Flesh of the Corpse</b></li> <li>Does Vicissitude have any effect on Werewolves/Fera, or would their regeneration fix it eventually? Like, would lowering or raising Appareance be undone by the regeneration? Organ, flesh and bone realignment be reversed by regeneration?</li> <li>Would a Vicissitude induced change be considered your default state for Life Sphere magic effects?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T07:02:09-07:00","id":1561682,"title":"","content":"1. Yes with caveats. By the rules it can't do so permanently without XP spending, it either just explains the effect or reduces XP cost if the ST is feeling generous.<br /> <br /> Other than that they probably rearrange things instead, solving one problem by causing other, which also fits with Vicissitude not creating tissue, so it has to work with what's already there.<br /> <br /> 2. Every change by Vicissitude is reversed as if it was Aggravated damage, so Shapechangers would regenerate everything back over time. They can't choose not to.<br /> <br /> That said, this is not as fast, so it isn't a complete waste of time.<br /> <br /> 3. That's hard to define. At first yes, the change is legit to the Pattern, but there's a grey area for Present vs Original vs Ideal Pattern, so I'd say it depends on Paradigm and effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T07:42:13-07:00","id":1561683,"title":"","content":"On the 3rd, my gut feeling it's that if it &quot;heals&quot; as aggravated damage then it's not really a <i>natural </i>change to the Pattern in the way Life Magic understands it.<br /> <br /> Think about it like this: You can heal Aggravated Damage on yourself with Life 2 (it costs Quintessence, but it's otherwise treated as normal damage), but you can't &quot;heal&quot; a natural disability at that level. Both are conditions that directly involve the Pattern (Agg it's damage to the Pattern), but one it's your default state and the other isn't<br /> <br /> It's a violent and unnatural change to the Pattern, that can be permanent (as unnatural spells can be Permanent), but it's not going to require a supernaturally Permanent transmutation to undo (one that would always be detected as magical, and can thus be Unweaved) - I would say it can be fixed with Life just like a Permanent Life 3+ &quot;alteration&quot; can be reversed with Life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-14-2026, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T09:23:25-07:00","id":1561686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561682#post1561682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Yes with caveats. By the rules it can't do so permanently without XP spending, it either just explains the effect or reduces XP cost if the ST is feeling generous.<br /> <br /> Other than that they probably rearrange things instead, solving one problem by causing other, which also fits with Vicissitude not creating tissue, so it has to work with what's already there.<br /> <br /> 2. Every change by Vicissitude is reversed as if it was Aggravated damage, so Shapechangers would regenerate everything back over time. They can't choose not to.<br /> <br /> That said, this is not as fast, so it isn't a complete waste of time.<br /> <br /> 3. That's hard to define. At first yes, the change is legit to the Pattern, but there's a grey area for Present vs Original vs Ideal Pattern, so I'd say it depends on Paradigm and effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, for 1, where are the XP costs stated for merits / flaws during play?<br /> <br /> I seem to remember that adquiring those was similar to Backgrounds, in that had to be roleplayed. But some other poster also mentioned XP cost in another thread for mage merits, so I am confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T11:50:37-07:00","id":1561727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561686#post1561686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, for 1, where are the XP costs stated for merits / flaws during play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere I ever saw in almost 30 years.<br /> <br /> I'd use 3 \u00d7 BP Value as a starting point.<br /> <br /> Another option is to have the player pay for the dots they bought originally with the BP gained. Never did that myself, but I do require my players to note down every purchase in a log, so we have a reference if we ever need to backtrack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T16:29:13-07:00","id":1561743,"title":"","content":"So in older editions, changes wrought by Vicissitude was generally permanent. It could be healed as Aggravated damage, both by vampires and other supernatural beings like werewoves, if you don't like the change. If you do like the change, then you can just keep it forever. It was possible to use it to get rid of certain character creation flaws such as the ones you mention. It can't get rid of clan curses, so a Nosferatu's appearance would go back to normal and a Cappadocian would start looking like a pale corpse again. Also, note that there was never any cost for removing flaws or getting merits post-character creation. <br /> <br /> So, using Vicissitude to get rid of flaws is a bit meta-gamey and something a lot of ST's never really liked. &quot;I'm going to take these flaws for bonus points and then since my character has Vicissitude, 5 seconds into the first sessions I'll permanently get rid of those flaws. Hooray for free BP!&quot;<br /> <br /> A common house rule is to make players buy off flaws that they got at character creation. So if you want to get rid of the Child flaw, you'd have to spend exp (usually x2-x3 the cost of the flaw). Otherwise the Vicissitude changes would not permanently take. <br /> <br /> Anyway, this was always more of a meta-gaming issue. How you want to do things would be up to your ST. Trying to game the system by getting free BP at character creation by taking flaws you plan to immediately get rid of is pretty frowned on. <br /> <br /> As for its actions with Life Sphere effects, I'd generally say no, Vicissitude wouldn't be treated as your natural state, but the effect of an outside curse. So utilizing certain Life Sphere effects would remove the Vicissitude effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T16:47:05-07:00","id":1561744,"title":"","content":"Instead of just making it cost x amount of xp to remove I would make it part of the story. It should take time for the character to learn how to use the power to alter themself in such a way to over come the flaws.<br /> <br /> I would go one of two routes:<br /> <br /> First would be a more direct route, requiring a Dex + Body Crafts roll at high Difficulty (10 or 11) Its hard to understand what is &quot;normal&quot; when you've never been &quot;normal&quot; yourself. Removing the Short flaw for example, may lead to the character in question over compensating and being Monsterous instead.<br /> <br /> Second would be an indirect route, where the character is taken out of play while they work on their self over time. During this time they lose out on benefits of play and xp gained by the rest of the troupe so it balances the initial BP gain.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Mages, they're just mortals so it should effect them like any other mortal initially, and then require a Time and Life effect to reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T17:23:02-07:00","id":1561747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561727#post1561727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nowhere I ever saw in almost 30 years.<br /> <br /> I'd use 3 \u00d7 BP Value as a starting point.<br /> <br /> Another option is to have the player pay for the dots they bought originally with the BP gained. Never did that myself, but I do require my players to note down every purchase in a log, so we have a reference if we ever need to backtrack.</div> </div> </div> </div>The M20 Core states:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 Core p. 642</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, Merits and Flaws cannot be purchased after<br /> character creation, although the Storyteller may decide to give<br /> them to characters in place of experience points if those Traits<br /> seem appropriate to the events within the chronicle. Depending<br /> upon those events, <b>a player might be able to use experience<br /> points to buy off a troublesome Flaw.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It tells us we can use XP to buy Flaws, but never shares the cost!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-15-2026, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T17:29:09-07:00","id":1561748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561744#post1561744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of just making it cost x amount of xp to remove I would make it part of the story. It should take time for the character to learn how to use the power to alter themself in such a way to over come the flaws.<br /> <br /> I would go one of two routes:<br /> <br /> First would be a more direct route, requiring a Dex + Body Crafts roll at high Difficulty (10 or 11) Its hard to understand what is &quot;normal&quot; when you've never been &quot;normal&quot; yourself. Removing the Short flaw for example, may lead to the character in question over compensating and being Monsterous instead.<br /> <br /> Second would be an indirect route, where the character is taken out of play while they work on their self over time. During this time they lose out on benefits of play and xp gained by the rest of the troupe so it balances the initial BP gain.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Mages, they're just mortals so it should effect them like any other mortal initially, and then require a Time and Life effect to reverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone here would ditch the roleplay for that. It's part of the story, period.<br /> <br /> But IME, while that isn't always the player trying to game the system, giving no cost is never a good idea unless something like that will happen to all the players, or the group had the idea, agreed and then asked you.<br /> <br /> Also, Fleshcraft already includes anatomical knowledge. Asking a master in anatomical adulteration that frequently starts with a normal target and must still have a functional result, to learn from impossible difficulties because they &quot;don't know what normal is&quot; seems pretty odd.<br /> <br /> Taking the character out of play IME is just not fun at all, unless the player already wanted to change characters for some sessions.<br /> <br /> You're not taking another route, you're asking for XP cost in another form, but one that also punishes the players by removing one for several sessions. And isn't making this a story, either, since it won't be told.<br /> <br /> Making it a hard, long-term project, as the Fleshcrafter studies how to tackle this particular case is, in fact, a good idea. But just inform up front how much it will cost and, at the end, take it. You can still roll dice if you want, if it fails there's no change and no cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561747#post1561747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The M20 Core states:<br /> <br /> <br /> It tells us we can use XP to buy Flaws, but never states the cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, since 2nd Edition at least. Exactly like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T15:43:07-07:00","id":1561852,"title":"","content":"Thanks<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26219\" data-vbnamecard=\"26219\">Aydoo</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a><br /> <br /> A final question, Vicissitude what is the maximum value that can put Appareance to? I understand some ratings based on Generation or equivalent, but there is no reason why a crafted Appareance for anyone (the user or a beneficiary).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T15:53:48-07:00","id":1561855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561852#post1561852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26219\" data-vbnamecard=\"26219\">Aydoo</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a><br /> <br /> A final question, Vicissitude what is the maximum value that can put Appareance to? I understand some ratings based on Generation or equivalent, but there is no reason why a crafted Appareance for anyone (the user or a beneficiary).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Appearance as an Attribute is a stupid rule.<br /> <br /> Which means there's no &quot;good&quot; answer. They're all equally terrible.<br /> <br /> That out of the way, I'd say above 5 the limit is the lower between the Fleshcrafter Discipline dots and the recipient's Species/Generation cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T17:01:43-07:00","id":1561857,"title":"","content":"On the 3rd point, I'd suggest to have in mind Vampire Storytellers Handbook crossover rules with Mage. On a mage's case it is sphere level vs. discipline level.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T17:37:54-07:00","id":1561860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561857#post1561857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the 3rd point, I'd suggest to have in mind Vampire Storytellers Handbook crossover rules with Mage. On a mage's case it is sphere level vs. discipline level.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with the Storyteller Handbooks is that they always benefit the line of the book, in this case Vampire (since achieving Discipline 5 is incredibly easier).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T20:19:02-07:00","id":1561867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561857#post1561857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the 3rd point, I'd suggest to have in mind Vampire Storytellers Handbook crossover rules with Mage. On a mage's case it is sphere level vs. discipline level.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be problematic on the 20th edition as the maximum level for spheres is 5, unless you use optional rules, so everyone with a 6th level power will triumph Mages, always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T23:02:52-07:00","id":1561872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561867#post1561867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would be problematic on the 20th edition as the maximum level for spheres is 5, unless you use optional rules, so everyone with a 6th level power will triumph Mages, always.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is Vampires. And Spirits.<br /> <br /> Very few Werewolves can have level 6 powers, usually one level 6 power. No one else. No one gets to 7 besides Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T23:33:18-07:00","id":1561875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561855#post1561855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Appearance as an Attribute is a stupid rule.<br /> <br /> Which means there's no &quot;good&quot; answer. They're all equally terrible.<br /> <br /> That out of the way, I'd say above 5 the limit is the lower between the Fleshcrafter Discipline dots and the recipient's Species/Generation cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second both these points.<br /> <br /> On to the previous discussion <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Fleshcraft already includes anatomical knowledge. Asking a master in anatomical adulteration that frequently starts with a normal target and must still have a functional result, to learn from impossible difficulties because they &quot;don't know what normal is&quot; seems pretty odd. </div> </div> </div>This is untrue. Vicissitude itself has no prerequisite to have any type of knowledge, just the same as someone with a dot of Celerity need to have a doctorate in going fast, or Potence with things getting hit hard. The anatomical knowledge is the purview of Body Crafts (altering the body) and Medicine (actual knowledge of the body.)<br /> <br /> Secondly we're talking about removing flaws. I'm going to assume you were born an average human being born with all your limbs, orifices, and at an average size/height. Lets use Short as our example flaw we are going to remove. Someone with this flaw isn't just below average 5ft / 152cm tall. They are either a child, or something like 3-4ft / 91-121cm tall. So from this character's POV, while yes they can see and understand that people have longer limbs, and are at an average height range, they are also going to have a hard time adjusting and trying to find a spot that doesn't either look weird or over-compensate into some kind of gangly noodle person. Remember as well Vicissitude is also (initially) only using the material that exists there to change the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T01:47:22-07:00","id":1561881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561875#post1561875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I second both these points.<br /> <br /> On to the previous discussion<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is untrue. Vicissitude itself has no prerequisite to have any type of knowledge, just the same as someone with a dot of Celerity need to have a doctorate in going fast, or Potence with things getting hit hard. The anatomical knowledge is the purview of Body Crafts (altering the body) and Medicine (actual knowledge of the body.)<br /> <br /> Secondly we're talking about removing flaws. I'm going to assume you were born an average human being born with all your limbs, orifices, and at an average size/height. Lets use Short as our example flaw we are going to remove. Someone with this flaw isn't just below average 5ft / 152cm tall. They are either a child, or something like 3-4ft / 91-121cm tall. So from this character's POV, while yes they can see and understand that people have longer limbs, and are at an average height range, they are also going to have a hard time adjusting and trying to find a spot that doesn't either look weird or over-compensate into some kind of gangly noodle person. Remember as well Vicissitude is also (initially) only using the material that exists there to change the body.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the edition. In V20, most Vicissitude powers use Medicine, which is a Knowledge. RAW, you can't attempt a roll with a Knowledge unless you have at least one dot in it. This is less of an issue in Revised, where Body Crafts is a variant of the Crafts Skill, and so is merely rolled at a small difficulty penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T03:35:28-07:00","id":1561884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561680-v20-vicissitude-questions-flaws-other-supernaturals?p=1561875#post1561875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is untrue. Vicissitude itself has no prerequisite to have any type of knowledge, just the same as someone with a dot of Celerity need to have a doctorate in going fast, or Potence with things getting hit hard. The anatomical knowledge is the purview of Body Crafts (altering the body) and Medicine (actual knowledge of the body.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not precisely because you need an Ability to put it to use.<br /> <br /> The usual Fleshcrafter that's trying such a feat is expected to have dots in the Ability (be it Body Crafts or Medicine) and reasonable experience, which means experience both making drastic alterations and altering the bodies of others.<br /> <br /> Your proposal emulates how hard it would be for a complete newbie without training, but applying to a regular roll as used by a professional.<br /> <br /> A Fleshcrafter with no experience at all with a variety of bodies and no notion of a normal body is already someone with no Ability dots and Attribute likely low to mid, throwing 2 or 3 dice at Diff +1 if it's a Craft, no roll at all of it is a Knowledge, as adambeyoncelowe said. This character will likely fail regardless.<br /> <br /> Given that this was not the only problem, I don't think, for very real, that a Diff 10-11 makes any sense whatsoever when you already can turn people into furniture while keeping the body functional and alive at way lower Dif.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}